{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Patel, one of the OB-GYN doctors here. You were brought in last night from the emergency department. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I’ve been hearing voices. They keep saying something bad is going to happen to my baby. I was so scared."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:17:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m so sorry you’re going through that. That must have been really frightening. Did you feel like the voices were telling you to hurt yourself or the baby?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not to hurt anyone. But they just keep repeating that something bad will happen. I called my OB because I felt less movement earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:18:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And how’s the baby’s movement now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s back to normal. I can feel kicks again. But the voices won’t stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:19:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thank you for sharing that. We’ve checked the baby’s heart rate, and it’s strong and normal. No signs of distress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good… but why am I hearing these things? I’ve been trying so hard to stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of bipolar disorder and previous hospitalizations, the psychiatry team thinks this might be a manic episode, possibly with psychosis related to your pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:21:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Psychosis? Like… losing touch with reality?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:22:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it’s treatable. It can happen during pregnancy, especially with a history like yours. The good news is we can help manage it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t taken my Haldol today. My psychiatrist started it last week, but I was nervous about the side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:23:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. The team knows. They’ve recommended restarting it at a higher dose to help with the voices and agitation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:24:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt the baby?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve weighed the risks. Untreated psychosis poses a greater risk to both you and the baby. Haldol is considered relatively safe in pregnancy when needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-01-22 08:25:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I trust you. I just want to be well for my baby."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. The psychiatrist spoke with you earlier, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Dr. Lee. She said I meet criteria for acute mania with psychotic features. She increased my Haldol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. You’ll get 2 mg twice today, and then 4 mg at night. We’ll also give you Ativan if you feel too anxious or restless."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:33:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did feel really agitated last night. My heart was racing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your heart rate was in the 110s when you arrived. But it’s calmer now. Your labs also showed a slightly high white blood cell count, but no infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the stress?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:35:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We also saw your bicarbonate was low, which can happen with dehydration or stress. We’re giving you fluids to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been eating much. I’ve been too anxious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-01-22 10:37:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll keep you on IV fluids for now and help you get back to regular meals. Your prenatal vitamins are still important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The voices are quieter. I still hear them, but not as loud. And I slept better last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. The Haldol and Ativan are helping. The psychiatry team is pleased."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’m still worried. Am I going to be okay to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing much better, but because of your history of suicide attempts, the team thinks you’d benefit from a few more days in a specialized psychiatric unit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m not going home yet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:05:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not directly home, no. But it’s not because you’re not improving. It’s to make sure your medications are fully adjusted in a safe place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I see… and the baby? Will I be able to stay with the baby?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:07:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still pregnant, so you’ll be in a maternal psychiatric facility. They’re equipped to care for both you and your baby. You’ll have regular OB check-ins."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-01-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was afraid I’d be separated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Today’s the day. The facility has a bed ready for you. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Nervous, but okay. The voices are almost gone now. I feel more like myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. Your vitals are stable, the baby is doing well, and your mental status has cleared. You’re alert and coherent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What meds will I be on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue Haldol—2 mg in the morning, 4 mg at night—and Buspar twice daily. Also, 1 mg of Ativan at bedtime for sleep, plus your prenatal vitamins and Zantac for reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my asthma?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:05:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You haven’t had any wheezing, so just keep your inhaler with you. Use it if you need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. For everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing the right thing by getting this support. The facility will help you stay stable for the rest of your pregnancy. You’ve got this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so. I just want to be a good mom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-01-24 10:08:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you will be. Asking for help is part of being a good mom. We’ll make sure you get the care you need."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-01-24 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team will be here soon to take you. Your OB will follow up with the facility, and you’ll have appointments lined up after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-01-24 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I call my family when I get there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-01-24 11:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. They’ll help you set up visitation and calls. You’re not alone in this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-01-24 11:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’m scared, but I feel safer knowing I’m getting help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-01-24 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. You’re taking a brave step. We’ll keep in touch with your care team. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-01-22 08:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-01-24 15:54:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old pregnant woman with a history of bipolar disorder and prior psychiatric hospitalizations was admitted for a manic episode with psychotic features, presenting with auditory hallucinations concerning harm to her fetus. She had no obstetric complications, and fetal monitoring remained reassuring throughout. She was evaluated by psychiatry, restarted on haloperidol, and treated for agitation with lorazepam and supportive care, including IV fluids for mild dehydration. Her symptoms improved significantly, and due to her psychiatric history and ongoing risk, she was transferred to an inpatient psychiatric facility for continued medication management and stabilization. She was discharged in stable mental and physical condition with a clear plan for follow-up care.",
    "problems": [
      "Mental disorders of mother, antepartum condition or complication",
      "Bipolar I disorder, most recent episode (or current) depressed, severe, specified as with psychotic behavior",
      "Dehydration",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other current conditions classifiable elsewhere of mother, antepartum condition or complication"
    ]
  }
}
